    },
    {
      "text": "Uniform incorporation of graphene nanoplatelets into a high-entropy-alloy matrix will reduce its wear rate.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The friction and wear reductions will persist across a wide service-temperature range.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Powder metallurgy can produce an even dispersion of graphene nanoplatelets in the high-entropy-alloy matrix.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Applied stress and temperature cause embedded graphene nanoplatelets to exfoliate and align at the sliding interface.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The exfoliated and aligned graphene forms a continuous, low-shear-strength tribofilm.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The graphene-derived tribofilm adheres to the sliding interface.",
